Subagents

Subagents are specialized assistants that Claude Code can delegate tasks to.
Think of them as focused helpers: each one runs in its own conversation context window, does its work, and returns a summary to the main thread.
The intermediate steps -- all the file reads, searches, and tool calls -- stay isolated and never clutter your main conversation.

Subagents spinn up a separate context window. The subagent's starting context includes:

1. A custom system prompt from your configuration file that defines the subagent's role and behavior
2. A task description written by the parent agent based on what you asked for

The subagent then works on its own. 
It reads files, runs searches, edits code -- whatever it needs to do.
When it's done, only a summary comes back to your main conversation. Claude Code saves the rest of the subagent's conversation in a separate transcript file.


This means your main context stays clean. You get the answer without all the noise of the journey it took to find it. 
The tradeoff is that your main conversation doesn't see how the subagent reached its conclusions.

Built-in Subagents

General purpose subagent -- for multi-step tasks that require both exploration and action
Explore -- for fast searching and navigation of codebases
Plan -- used during plan mode for research and analysis of your codebase before presenting a plan
